==Finnish==

===Etymology===
{{glossary|haplology|Haplologically}} from earlier {{m|fi|inhiminen}} (compare {{m|fi|inhimillinen}}), from {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*inhiminen}} (compare {{cog|et|inimene}}, {{cog|krl|ihmini}}), possibly from {{der|fi|urj-fpr-pro|*inše}} (compare {{cog|myv|инже||guest}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p|a=fi-ihminen.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[human]], [[human being]] {{gl|an individual}}
# [[man]], [[Homo sapiens]]
#: {{ux|fi|'''Ihminen''' on kädellinen nisäkäs.|'''Man''' is a primate mammal.}}
# {{synonym of|fi|henkilö||person}}

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-nainen|ihmi|ä}}

